{"id": "EUVD-2026-102322", "enisaUuid": "50c9247b-9ddc-32ba-8e39-e764671d0241", "description": "A flaw was found in the internal WebAssembly (WASM) shim used by the Kuadrant operator. When generating the CEL predicate that determines whether Gateway-level authentication and rate limiting should run, the shim does not correctly escape values from HTTPRoute match fields. A user who can create or modify an HTTPRoute attached to a shared Gateway can provide a crafted path, header, or query match value that causes the predicate to skip those checks. The request is still forwarded to the route\u2019s backend.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:44:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T05:03:49", "baseScore": 7.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:L", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:83531", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:88203", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-108334", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2548768", "https://github.com/Kuadrant/kuadrant-operator/commit/7e667dc216e6ad38feaeadb391da59aa0380057a", "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-fcw2-f6v9-6ffp"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108334", "GHSA-fcw2-f6v9-6ffp"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.33, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "11762b12-f75e-30a8-a0c5-d3a55a06eb35", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Connectivity Link 1.4", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1791975888"}, {"id": "edb7500b-6b90-3db6-a00d-1ea22bf71450", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Connectivity Link 1.5", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1792512519"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2e9934a6-03a9-3904-a4c6-1ce1b1f41338", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}], "isExploited": false}